# The Adaptive Engagement Framework

Official research code, dataset, and supporting materials for the study:

**The adaptive engagement framework: enhancing banking customer experience through AI-powered invisible marketing**

Published in *Scientific Reports* (2026).

## Overview

This repository contains the dataset, source code, and supporting materials used to implement the computational experiments reported in the study.

The proposed framework investigates customer interaction propensity in digital banking using machine learning and deep learning approaches. The computational workflow includes data preprocessing, feature preparation, feature-to-image conversion, convolutional neural network classification, and performance evaluation.

The repository is intended to support transparency and reproducibility of the computational experiments presented in the associated publication.

## Dataset

The repository includes the processed dataset used for the computational experiments:

```text
BankDataSet_Processed.xlsx
```

The dataset contains customer-level records used for model development and evaluation.

Researchers using the dataset should comply with all applicable data protection, privacy, ethical, and institutional requirements. The dataset is provided for academic and research purposes only.

## Source Code

The main implementation files included in the repository are:

### Feature-to-Image Conversion

```text
Feature to image conversion.py
```

This script converts the prepared tabular feature representation into image-based representations suitable for convolutional neural network analysis.

The generated image representations are subsequently used as inputs to the CNN classification pipeline.

### CNN Classification Pipeline

```text
Cnn classification pipeline.py
```

This script implements the CNN-based classification pipeline used in the study, including model training and evaluation procedures.

The pipeline uses the image representations generated by the feature-to-image conversion script and performs the subsequent deep learning classification and performance evaluation.

## Requirements

The required Python packages are listed in:

```text
requirements.txt
```

Install the required dependencies using:

```bash
pip install -r requirements.txt
```

## Workflow

The main computational workflow can be summarized as follows:

```text
Processed Dataset
       ↓
Data Preprocessing
       ↓
Feature Preparation
       ↓
Feature-to-Image Conversion
       ↓
Image-Based Representation
       ↓
CNN Classification
       ↓
Model Evaluation
       ↓
Performance Analysis
```

The feature-to-image conversion script should be executed before the CNN classification pipeline because the generated image representations serve as inputs to the CNN models.

